1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
Rationalize 1 over the cube root of 5.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:10,733
Multiply by ∛5? Below you'd get ∛25: still a radical.

3
00:00:10,733 --> 00:00:14,933
A cube root clears when the exponent inside reaches 3.

4
00:00:14,933 --> 00:00:18,867
5¹ fills just one slot.

5
00:00:18,867 --> 00:00:24,867
So multiply by the cube root of 5²: 1 + 2 = 3…

6
00:00:24,867 --> 00:00:28,967
…and the cube root of 5³ is 5.

7
00:00:28,967 --> 00:00:33,667
Answer: ∛25 / 5.

8
00:00:33,667 --> 00:00:37,467
Harder: the 7th root of 1 over a².

9
00:00:37,467 --> 00:00:41,000
a² fills 2 of 7 slots…

10
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,633
…so multiply by the 7th root of a⁵.

11
00:00:46,633 --> 00:00:49,233
Fill the exponent up to n…

12
00:00:49,233 --> 00:00:53,100
…and the root clears.
